ii. Economic feasibility report or market analysis;
iii. Area traffic study and circulation plan within the development and to and from existing thoroughfares;
iv. Hydraulic, hydrologic, and drainage engineering studies;
v. Environmentally sensitive areas, including, but not limited to: watershed protection, wetlands, or groundwater recharge impact study; and
vi. Based on the pre-application meeting with the zoning administrator, other information as is deemed necessary may be requested; in addition, any of the aforementioned required information (items (a) thru (h)) may be excluded if deemed not applicable.
